    {
      "source": "Doctors of Running",
      "priority": 3,
      "url": "https://www.doctorsofrunning.com/2025/06/saucony-hurricane-25-review-2025.html",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: The dual-layer PWRRUN PB/PWRRUN midsole is very soft and highly cushioned, with strong impact protection and a notably compressive heel; the forefoot feels smooth with mild flexibility but can turn mushy at slower paces.",
        "Responsiveness: Energy return is strong for a stability shoe, with clear bounce from the PWRRUN PB that improves at normal-to-uptempo paces and with longer strides, but it is less snappy for easy recovery running.",
        "Stability: Stability is mild-to-moderate, supported by medial heel guidance, a rigid heel counter, secure lockdown, and a generally non-flexible platform; however, the softer foam and deeper heel compression make it less stable than firmer options.",
        "Durability: Expected durability is above average, aided by extensive XT-900 outsole coverage and generally durable materials, though outsole performance shows only average traction and some wet-surface slipping."
      ]
    },
    {
      "source": "Believe in the Run",
      "priority": 5,
      "url": "https://believeintherun.com/shoe-reviews/saucony-hurricane-25-review/",
      "type": "qualitative",
      "keyFindings": [
        "Cushioning: Max-cushion setup (38/32 mm) with PWRRUN + PWRRUN PB feels soft and protective, with a comfortable underfoot squish in both heel and forefoot that keeps legs feeling fresher.",
        "Responsiveness: Reviewers noted more pop and a bouncier ride than v24; the PB-heavy feel adds energy return and can pull easy runs toward faster cruising paces.",
        "Stability: CenterPath design (higher sidewalls, rocker geometry, wide base, sole flare) delivers strong but non-intrusive guidance; platform felt secure with good pronation control and lateral confidence.",
        "Durability: Direct wear/longevity testing is not reported; XT-900 outsole is listed, but the review provides no concrete outsole-wear or long-term material durability findings."
      ]
    }
